{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]First time I seen my true [F]Iove,
[C]he was walkin' by my door,[G]
the last [C]time l saw his false hearted [F]smile,
he was dead on [G]his coolin' board.[C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It's a-hard [C]and it's hard, ain't it hard,[F]
to [C]love one that never did love you?[G]
It's a-hard, [C]and it's hard, ain't it hard, great [F]God,
to [G]love one that never [G7]will be true?[C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]There is a house in this town,[F]
[C]that's where my true love lays around.[G]
He takes [C]other women right down on his knee,[F]
he [G]tells them a little tale he won't tell me.[C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Don't go to drinkin' and gamblin',[F]
don't go [C]there your sorrows to drown.[G]
This [C]hard-liquor place is a low-down [F]disgrace,
it's [G]the meanest damn place in this town.[C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
It was late [C]last night, when my true love come [F]in,
[C]rapped, and knocked upon my door.[G]
[C]I jumped out in a fit of [F]jealousy,
that true [G]love don’t knock here any more.[C]
{end_of_verse}
